ely due to the delay cap: even with unbounded waiting, 798 reaches 651 nodes but 131 is not among them (step_02), and 131's only in-neighbours are 368, 972, 1877, 1932 (step_05) \u2014 368, 972 and 1877 are unreachable from 798 (step_07, step_14, step_15), while 1932 is reachable only via multi-hop lags of 5432/5024/11927 units (step_08), an order of magnitude beyond the 600-unit criterion, and that arrival at t=33775 comes after 131's activity has effectively ceased (step_10). Confounders are controlled: the graph is busy (4959 events, 1888 active nodes, step_03) and a static, order-ignoring connection between the two neighbourhoods does exist (step_11, including 389->131), yet both nodes are individually sparse (5 and 8 events, step_04) and their activity bins barely overlap in a usable order (step_09, step_10). Static connectivity plus ambient volume therefore explain the apparent link; the temporal ordering does not support a genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_6f333458\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [798, 131],\n  \"window\": [4302, 42701],\n  \"confidence\": 0.93,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Under the 600-unit relay constraint, node 798 reaches only 4 nodes in the whole interval and never 131 (step_01); no time-respecting path is enumerable (step_12). The failure is not merely due to the delay cap: even with unbounded waiting, 798 reaches 651 nodes but 131 is not among them (step_02), and 131's only in-neighbours are 368, 972, 1877, 1932 (step_05) \u2014 368, 972 and 1877 are unreachable from 798 (step_07, step_14, step_15), while 1932 is reachable only via multi-hop lags of 5432/5024/11927 units (step_08), an order of magnitude beyond the 600-unit criterion, and that arrival at t=33775 comes after 131's activity has effectively ceased (step_10). Confounders are controlled: the graph is busy (4959 events, 1888 active nodes, step_03) and a static, order-ignoring connection between the two neighbourhoods does exist (step_11, including 389->131), yet both nodes are individually sparse (5 and 8 events, step_04) and their activity bins barely overlap in a usable order (step_09, step_10). Static connectivity plus ambient volume therefore explain the apparent link; the temporal ordering does not support a genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 39092, "total_output_tokens": 3649, "total_tokens": 42741, "total_latency_ms": 49669, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}